module ConnectRpcRails
  # Reads a protobuf ServiceDescriptor (generated by protoc/buf and present in the
  # descriptor pool) into the RPC table the transport dispatches from. Dispatch is
  # reflection-based: the action names and the input/output message classes come
  # entirely from the descriptor, so no per-service code generation is required.
  #
  # The service is named the way the `.proto` names it — `"greet.v1.GreetService"` — and
  # looked up in the pool, so the string in the code is greppable from the protobuf
  # definition. A ServiceDescriptor is accepted too, for a host that already holds one.
  #
  # The service is implemented by the controller itself — the RPC methods are ordinary
  # controller instance methods. There is deliberately no handler object: a handler held
  # on the controller class would be one instance shared by every request in the process,
  # so leftover instance state could leak between callers, whereas Rails builds a
  # controller per request.
